# Drives a full sim run like a person would, through the same protocol the mod uses.
# Usage (Foreman running with --backend sim --reset):
#   npm run tui -- --script scripts/sim-demo.script --transcript ../artifacts/logs/foreman_sim.txt
# Decision ids are deterministic on a fresh profile: d1 permission, d2/d3 merge t2 (changes
# requested on d2), d4 merge t4, d5 question, d6 merge t3, d7 merge t5, d8 merge t6,
# d9 question (what to do with the blocked npm publish task t7).
/status
Add #tags to pocket-notes: parse them, filter with `notes list --tag`, and show a `notes tags` summary
/wait d1
/wait 1.5
/answer d1 3
/wait d2
/diff kit-t2
/wait 2
/answer d2 2 Please add a doc comment for normalizeTag
/wait d3
@kit thanks - nice regex work
/answer d3 1
/wait d4
/wait d5
/pause @juniper
/stop @tove
/wait 2
/status
/resume @juniper
/resume @tove
/answer d5 2
/answer d4 1
/wait d6
/wait d7
/diff juniper-t3
/wait 2
/answer d6 1
/answer d7 1
/wait d8
/agents
/answer d8 Merge
/wait d9
/answer d9 1
/wait goal done
/wait 1
/status
/memory shared/plan
/memory shared/decisions
/counts
/quit
